A||||9||cadero2dmax||GRM Loves everyone||||1||
Z||000000||cadero2dmax||12-18-2001||05:45 AM||||While perusing the autocrossing mailing list, I ran into an article by the editor of Grassroots Motorsports Magazine, a copy of which follows my correspondence to him.<P>I have copy/pasted my letter of response, and am posting it here for your review/comments. PFF members could even write their own letters to substantialte mine, if you would like.<P><BR>---------------------------------------<BR>(Private response to a message posted to Team.Net)<BR> <BR>I am trying to throw together a 4.9 Cadillac powered Fiero for the $2002 Challenge just to get a photo of one somewhere in the background in your mag!! <BR> <BR>I have yet to see a Fiero featured at all in your magazine. My quad 4 Fiero was racing in the SCCA all over the MidWest in GT-2 in it's early years, and both autocrossing and ProSolo since 1992  (until last year when I sold it). <BR>It is currently in Tucson frequently earning FTD against the likes of National Champion Corvette drivers, Formula Fords, etc. <BR> <BR>I wrote to GRM on a couple occasion asking for coverage on this car (a photo is attached), or any other  Fiero. My intent was to address the misclassing of the Fiero by the SCCA in all categories (except E-Mod of course). But since it HAS been mis-classed since 1993 with the introduction of the Miata, the Fiero has never gained any notoriety - and thus not material for a feature car in your magazine. <BR> <BR>On another occasion Per asked Team.Net for a car owner willing to dedicate a week for fine tuning the suspension and improve the handling (A little over a year or so ago if I recall) at Atlanta Motor Speedway. I volunteered my Fiero and was not even given the dignity of a response !<BR> <BR>There are multiple Fieros out there racing with stock powerplants, Northstars, Small Blocks, Turbo or Supercharged 3.8's, 3.4's (both 3.4 engines, the standard and twin cam) quad 4's - - just about any GM powerplant including big blocks have been put in these little cars. Tamandli has won 5 National Championships in E-mod with his Fiero bodied (Rover/Buick powered) car. Never any coverage by GRM!!<BR> <BR>In this last issue, a V8 powered Nissan Z car is featured.yet you can't show me a single feature in your magazine in the past decade about any Pontiac Fiero, let alone a V8 powered one (such as my 4.9 Cad powered dual purpose daily driver/autocross car). You and your crew have completely ignored this fun to drive mid-engine AMERICAN car (the ONLY American mid engined car ever built) that had the first space frame  - - and a host of other innovations introduced to the U.S by this marquee. <BR> <BR>This marquee has a strong following, yet has been shunned by your magazine since I have been a subscriber - which is about 8 or 9 years. Over two years ago I  founded the Fiero Racing List, which currently has over 230 members nationwide, and whom I am Cc:ing this correspondence. Any one of their cars would make an interesting feature. We have at least one ProRally car, several ITA and ITB cars, a couple big-time 9 second drag cars, and a host of autocrossers in our fold.<BR> <BR>Let me know if any of our cars sound interesting enough for a feature in Grassroots Motorsports Magazine.<BR> <BR>George Ryan<BR> <BR>------------------------------<P>On Sun, 16 Dec 2001 at  22:08:20 EST David S. Wallens wrote to Autox.team.net:<P>&gt; Just wanted to publicly thank Per for explaining our situation. <BR>&gt; Truth of the matter is that we really love all cars--and that makes <BR>&gt; it tough to get everyone into the magazine, even if we're up to <BR>&gt; 172 pages and now printing eight times a year. I wish I got a <BR>&gt; dollar every time I lie awake at night wondering if the next issue <BR>&gt; is balanced enough: Do we have enough autocross coverage? <BR>&gt; What about rally? Too many Triumphs? Not enough vintage? <BR>&gt; Do we need to get another Camaro into the mag? Have we been <BR>&gt; keeping the Mustang guys happy? Do we have too much or not <BR>&gt; enough Honda info? Is this issue's tech piece hardcore enough? <BR>&gt; Do we have vintage coverage from both the East and West <BR>&gt; coasts? Is it time for another big piece on the Neon?<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; So, we do our best to push everyone's hot buttons, and we if <BR>&gt; skipped anyone, there no animosity on our part. We're just trying <BR>&gt; to make a well-rounded, informative, fun-to-read publication. <BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; If anyone ever has a questions or comments about the mag, feel <BR>&gt; free to e-mail me directly at grmdavid@aol.com. I get the digest <BR>&gt; version of team.net, but direct e-mail is the best way to reach me <BR>&gt; by far. <BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; Here's a hint for everyone: If you have a car that you think should <BR>&gt; be featured in the mag (like an ESP car, for example), let me know. <BR>&gt; You'd be amazed how many cars are featured somewhere in our <BR>&gt; magazine simply because someone took the time to contact us.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt; David S. Wallens, managing ed<BR>&gt; Grassroots Motorsports<BR>&gt; <A HREF="http://www.grassrootsmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.grassrootsmotorsports.com</A> <P>------------------------------<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Texas_Motor_Speedway.jpg">  <P><p>[This message has been edited by cadero2dmax (edited 12-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||12-18-2001||09:10 AM||||GRM has had Fieros in it in the past - usually as small, sidebar reviews of a car, or as part of a comparison article.  The car has not fared well in their editorials.  I believe GRM's general summary of the Fiero is that the '84-'87 cars are lousy autocrossers and that the '88's show some promise, but are too heavy.<P>Hopefully you can prove them wrong with your challenge car!  I look forward to hearing more about this as it progresses.<P>Good luck,<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||8
Z||000002||cadero2dmax||12-18-2001||05:44 PM||||The only one I remember is a comparison of Sports cars under $5,000. It was in that blurb that the statements you allude to about weight, etc was made (if I recall). I do not ever remember seeing a feature article, however in his response David Wallins said he did one in 1990. And i don't remember seeing a picture of a Fiero in his rag.<P>I am running out of time to do this car for the Challenge. I really need to find an '88 donor so I legally can run it in SM2 this year, but the 86 with an '88 cradle is all I could scrounge up. I still have a good chance at the February meet, but if I find too many more glitches will have to build for $2003 instead.<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hartz||12-18-2001||07:02 PM||||I have a box of old "Fiero related" magazines - later this week I will try to dig through it and see what I can't find on the Fiero in GRM.  I know I have at least 2-3 GRM's in the pile.<P>Sorry to hear about your troubles with the challenge car.  I think it is an awesome idea.  I remember when I first read the $1500 challenge mentally trying to build a Fiero.  Hopefully you will get things sorted and be able to give it a go.<P>Best of luck,<BR>Hartz||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadero2dmax||12-19-2001||07:15 AM||||I am surprised that the Fiero community does't care about being shunned like this.<P>But corresponcence with the GRM editor has opened the door to coverage of the PowerFest (if it ever happens) or perhaps even Ed's swap meet. We will see.<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hartz||12-19-2001||08:09 AM||||Well, my thoughts:<P>1)  Fieros have ALWAYS been shunmed by the media (among others).  I suspect most long time Fiero owners are used to this by now.<P>2)  I doubt half the folks on here even know what GRM is, as a magazine.  They're a niche player compared to large scale rags like C&D, MT, Hot Rod, Car Craft, etc.<P>Hartz||||reg||1
Z||000006||LZeitgeist||12-19-2001||08:21 AM||||Agreed, Hartz, on both points.<P>It's the flip-side of owning GM's 'bastard child'. No respect from anybody who isn't already a fan or enthusiast.<P>Heck with 'em - their disinterest keeps Fiero prices low for the rest of us.||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadero2dmax||12-20-2001||07:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Hartz:<BR><B>Well, my thoughts:<P>1)  Fieros have ALWAYS been shunmed by the media (among others).  I suspect most long time Fiero owners are used to this by now.<P>2)  I doubt half the folks on here even know what GRM is, as a magazine.  They're a niche player compared to large scale rags like C&D, MT, Hot Rod, Car Craft, etc.<P>Hartz</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's why all the excitement (and numerous posts) when some obscure Pontiac Performance magazine did a small article about a mildly modified Fiero?<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cheever3000||12-20-2001||10:07 PM||||It's true that I knew nothing about them until the $2002 Challenge, but I looked at the link you gave for their website and the first thing I noticed was at the top.  Their subtitle is "America's Sports Car Magazine".  How can they make that claim and exclude Fieros as you say they do?  <P>I was a little confused by your first post - was the first part your reply to Mr. Wallens' letter in the second part?  If so, (1)-They certainly appear to contradict themselves; and (2)-You said it all, how can we improve on that?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Well, I am going to do some reading of their website, maybe subscribe to the magazine (if you recommend it), and write some letters myself.  Fiero racers are getting the shaft from everyone, and their time has come.  Watch out, GRM!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CheeverXmasSig.jpg">   <BR><I>Merry Christmas from the </I><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank><I>CFOG-I</I></A> <I>vice-president.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadero2dmax||12-20-2001||10:52 PM||||Yes, my reply was first, then a copy of the editors letter from autox.team.net<P>Their magazine is one of the best for getting info about cars for autocrossing, rallying, and amatuer road racing. A lot of resources for lightweight wheels, racing brakes - - a lot of stuff the Fiero can use.<P>G||||reg||1
